  data: {
    LLM: "Hand selection is similar to Omaha but weaker because you can't use 3 cards. Look for hands that interact well with the board using 2 cards. Avoid 'tri-hand' traps (hands that need all 3 hole cards to be good).\n\nSince you can use 0 or 1 card, you aren't forced to use 2 like in Omaha. This makes one-card flushes and straights possible if the board allows. However, holding 3 cards gives more combinations.\n\nIn High-Low split, aim for scooping. A2x is a strong start for low. Keep in mind the 'Lazy Pineapple' aspectâ€”you keep all 3 cards till the end, giving you more information about what's NOT in the deck.",
